# Design Feedback — Resume Scoring Tool Landing Page

## The Problem

Both the resume tool and the B-Roll guide page were clearly built by an LLM because they share the exact same default AI design stack. Anyone who's seen a few AI-generated sites will clock it instantly. Here's what's identical:

---

## Shared AI Tells (What to Fix)

### 1. Font Stack — THE biggest tell
Both pages use the exact same combo:
- **DM Sans** for body/UI text
- **Instrument Serif** (italic) for the accent word ("Unfiltered" / "Custom Visuals")
- **DM Mono** for small labels

This is the #1 default font combo that Claude/ChatGPT reach for when building dark premium-looking sites. It's become the "tell me you used AI without telling me" of web design.

**Fix:** Replace with any of these combos:
- Headings: `"Suisse Intl", "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, sans-serif` → clean, Swiss, financial
- Accent/italic: `"Playfair Display"` or `"Cormorant Garamond"` instead of Instrument Serif
- Body: `"IBM Plex Sans"` or `"Söhne"` or just `"Helvetica Neue"` instead of DM Sans
- Mono: `"JetBrains Mono"` or `"SF Mono"` instead of DM Mono

### 2. The Italic Serif Accent Word
Using one gold/blue italic serif word inside a sans-serif heading ("Built for IB recruiting. *Unfiltered.*") is an AI layout cliche at this point. Every AI-generated landing page does this.

**Fix:** Either:
- Make the entire heading serif (not just one word)
- Use weight contrast instead of font contrast (e.g., light weight + bold weight, same font)
- If keeping the accent word, use a different serif than Instrument Serif and consider using color alone (no italic) to differentiate

### 3. Border Radius
Both pages use `8px` and `10px` border-radius — the AI default. Real premium/financial sites use sharper corners.

**Fix:**
- Cards/containers: `4px` max, or `2px` for that Bloomberg feel
- Buttons: `4px` or `2px` (not `8px`)
- Input fields: `2px` or `0px` (sharp)

### 4. Background Color
Both use nearly identical dark navy/charcoal backgrounds (`rgb(10,12,18)` on B-Roll, similar near-black on resume tool). This specific shade of dark is the AI default "dark mode."

**Fix:**
- Go true black: `#000000` or `#050505` — more confident, less "themed"
- Or go slightly warm: `#0C0A09` (warm black) instead of blue-tinted dark
- Avoid the navy-tinted dark that AI defaults to

### 5. Text Color / Opacity Pattern
Both use the same muted gray text (`rgb(184,191,206)` — a blue-gray) for body copy. This is the AI default "dark mode readable text."

**Fix:**
- Use a warmer gray: `#A8A29E` (stone) or `#9CA3AF` (neutral gray) instead of blue-gray
- Or go higher contrast: `#D4D4D4` for body text — more Bloomberg terminal, less AI template

### 6. Spacing Uniformity
AI-generated pages have eerily perfect, uniform spacing. Everything is multiples of 8px with identical gaps.

**Fix:**
- Introduce slight asymmetry — e.g., more padding on left than right in the hero
- Vary vertical spacing (don't make every section gap identical)
- Let the form card sit slightly higher or lower than perfectly centered

### 7. The "Continue →" Button
Gold/amber filled button with an arrow is a very common AI premium template pattern.

**Fix:**
- Consider an outlined/ghost button instead (border only, no fill)
- Or make it white text on transparent with a subtle border
- Remove the arrow `→` — it's an AI cliche. Just say "Continue" or "Submit"

---

## Quick Wins (Copy-Paste CSS Overrides)

```css
/* FONTS — swap the AI defaults */
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600&family=Cormorant+Garamond:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400&display=swap');

/* Replace DM Sans everywhere */
body, p, span, label, input {
  font-family: "IBM Plex Sans", "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em; /* tighter than AI default */
}

/* Replace Instrument Serif accent */
.accent-text, .italic-highlight {
  font-family: "Cormorant Garamond", Georgia, serif;
}

/* Replace DM Mono */
code, .mono, .stat-label {
  font-family: "JetBrains Mono", "SF Mono", monospace;
}

/* BORDER RADIUS — sharpen everything */
.card, .form-container {
  border-radius: 3px; /* was 8-10px */
}

button, input {
  border-radius: 2px; /* was 8px */
}

/* BACKGROUND — true black, not navy */
body, .hero {
  background-color: #050505; /* was ~rgb(10,12,18) navy */
}

/* TEXT COLOR — warmer, not blue-gray */
body, p {
  color: #B5B0A8; /* warm stone instead of blue-gray */
}

h1, h2, .heading {
  color: #EDEDED; /* slightly off-white */
}

/* BUTTON — less AI, more minimal */
.cta-button {
  background: transparent;
  border: 1px solid #D4A853;
  color: #D4A853;
  border-radius: 2px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  font-size: 13px;
}
```

## Summary

The page concept is strong — the bank ticker, invite-only gating, and IB-specific scoring angle are all good. The issue is purely surface-level: the font stack, border-radius, and color choices are the exact same defaults that every AI tool spits out. Swap the fonts, sharpen the corners, warm up the grays, and it'll immediately stop reading as AI-generated.

